          <attvalue for="36" value="A rapid rise in aggregated investor assessments of cross‑Strait political and economic risk drives risk‑off re‑pricing, causing secondary‑market selloffs and repricing of default probability that widen credit spreads across corporate and non‑sovereign debt." />
